   "file": "TauCeti/Analysis/Complex/CauchyIntegralPolydisc.lean",
   "fix": "Add a public lemma, e.g. `DifferentiableAt.comp_update (h : DifferentiableAt \ud835\udd5c f y) (i : \u03b9) : DifferentiableAt \ud835\udd5c (fun x => f (update y i x)) (y i)`, stated for any `\ud835\udd5c` and any finite `\u03b9`, and use it at all three sites.",
   "issue": "General infrastructure is missing: the same argument (`DifferentiableAt.comp (y i) _ (hasFDerivAt_update y (y i)).differentiableAt` then `rw [update_eq_self]`) is inlined at lines 199-203 (`DifferentiableOn.torusIntegral_prod_sub_inv_smul`), 349-351 (`analyticOnNhd_iff_continuousOn_and_differentiableAt_update`) and 372-375 (`DifferentiableOn.analyticAt_of_finiteDimensional`). Its statement uses only Mathlib types and Mathlib has no such lemma, so users applying the new Osgood API to jointly differentiable functions must rebuild it.",
